  "manual_review": {
    "positive_findings": [
      "The source-backed bark PBR and separate opaque bark section are technically valid.",
      "Tapered trunk, scaffold, secondary, and terminal geometry creates a readable open-grown oak silhouette without a billboard core.",
      "The reversible HISM integration proves that a multi-section true-woody asset can be reviewed at all 24830 production oak proxy instances without changing runtime authority."
    ],
    "rejection_reasons": [
      "Leaf coverage is too sparse and dark, producing black card fragments instead of a continuous evergreen crown.",
      "Exposed limbs are geometrically repetitive and too cleanly forked at guide-eye distance.",
      "The branch atlas contains twig-heavy silhouettes and weak leaf mass, so adding cards would amplify the same artifact rather than close the fidelity gap.",
      "All five frames still read as synthetic terrain, water, foliage, and lighting and cannot serve as release media."
    ],
    "decision": "Reject v210 visual promotion. Retain only the bark maps, two-section authoring path, strict render-data gate, tapered woody topology, transient integration seam, and captures as technical evidence.",
    "next_required_visual_input": "A new dense, leaf-dominant live-oak cluster source with robust opacity coverage, several crown-age/form variants, less regular branch topology, controlled near/mid/far representation transitions, and named art/ecology review."
